WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.168
♪ ("THE HUNTER GETS CAPTURED
BY THE GAME" BY THE MARVELETTES
PLAYING) ♪

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:05.238
<i> ♪ What's this ol' world
 Comin' to? ♪</i>

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.273
<i>♪ Things just ain't the same ♪</i>

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:08.808
♪ ("YOU CAN'T BE FUNKY"
BY BUSH TETRAS PLAYING) ♪

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.511
NAN GOLDIN:<i> Photography's like
 a flash of euphoria,</i>

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.047
<i> and it gave me a voice.</i>

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.617
<i>Once I started sharing the work,</i>

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.886
<i> there was really
 heavy resistance...</i>

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.589
<i>especially from male artists
 and galleries,</i>

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.292
<i> who said,
 "This isn't photography.</i>

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.495
<i> Nobody photographs
 their own life."</i>

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.498
<i> ♪ Dance, dance, dance
 Talk, talk, talk ♪</i>

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:35.969
Photographer Nan Goldin, she's
a major name in the art world.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.738
 SPEAKER:<i> The work was
 incredibly political.</i>

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:42.075
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.011
NAN:<i> Probably my whole life's
 a struggle</i>

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.947
<i> to fight conformity
 and denial.</i>

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:50.316
NAN: (VIA MICROPHONE)
<i>A hundred thousand deaths!</i>

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.585
ACTIVISTS:
A hundred thousand deaths!

00:00:57.457 --> 00:01:00.093
PATRICK RADDEN KEEFE:
<i>There's the Sackler family
 of the art world,</i>

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.362
<i> the museum world,
 and philanthropy,</i>

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:05.197
and then there's
the Big Pharma marketing,

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:07.166
and addiction, and death.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:09.068
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:12.138
NAN:
<i>My anger at the Sackler family,</i>

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:13.639
<i> it's personal.</i>

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.710
<i>When you think of the profit
 off people's pain,</i>

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.745
<i> you can only be furious.</i>

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:24.451
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.787
NOEMI BONAZZI:
<i>Nan said, "I think we should
 take these people down,</i>

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.924
but do you think
my career will implode?"

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.291
And I said, "Probably."

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:36.395
We need to demand
that the Met Museum,
the Louvre, the Tate

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.964
refuse donations
from the Sacklers

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.266
and take down their name.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:44.369
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.905
NAN:
<i>The rich people are scared</i>

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:49.008
<i>that we're gonna dig into
the evil way they make money.</i>

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:52.345
ALL: Sacklers lie! Sacklers lie!

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:56.783
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:00.786
NAN:<i> When you grow up
being told, "that didn't happen,</i>

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:02.154
<i> you didn't see that,"</i>

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.856
<i>how do you trust yourself?</i>

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.893
<i> And so that's the reason
 I take pictures.</i>

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.295
SPEAKER 2:
<i>This is a watershed moment.</i>

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:12.131
<i>People are actually beginning
to rethink how they do things.</i>

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.700
ACTIVISTS: Say it loud!
Say it clear!

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.102
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.872
ACTIVISTS: No longer!
No longer! No longer!

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.875
NAN:<i> The wrong things
are kept secret in society,</i>

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.545
<i>and that destroys people.</i>

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.852 line:0%
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

